ted_at":1794491143,"finished_at":1794491151}},{"type":"text","data":{"text":"The error \"permission denied\" for `/./file` suggests the file is protected by system permissions or is a restricted system file. To resolve this, you can:\n\n1. **Check permissions** using `ls -l /./file` to confirm ownership and access rights.\n2. **Use `sudo`** to temporarily elevate privileges:  \n   ```bash\n   sudo view /./file\n   ```\n3. **Verify the file''s existence** with `ls /./file` to ensure it''s not a virtual file or a system artifact.\n\nIf the file is a system file, avoid modifying it unless instructed by an administrator."}},{"type":"finish","data":{"reason":"end_turn","time":1794491154}}]','qwen3:1.7b',1794491140,1794491154,1794491154,'ollama',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
